the buffer's header scan agrees with the list's on a response, on a body with no blank line, and on a blank line at the very end: True
a response fed 1,460 bytes at a time reads back byte for byte: True
the feed keeps exactly the first http-max-response bytes and no more, as the list did: True
a 2,000-byte response costs less than 1/100 of the 8 MiB the list reserved: True
